research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-159-{"id":"thm-regularity-of-the-alephs","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"I verified all four clauses against their cited facts. Step 1.1 correctly derives cf(aleph_0)=aleph_0 from L1, L4, L9. Step 1.2 correctly constructs the cofinal set C={aleph_n} and computes |C|=aleph_0. Step 1.3 correctly sets up the contradiction for clause (b): beta=cf(kappa) is an infinite cardinal below the successor cardinal, hence beta<=lambda. Step 2.1 correctly squeezes cf(aleph_omega) between aleph_0 and aleph_0. Step 2.2 correctly uses AC (L8) to select injections e_xi, constructs an injection kappa -> beta x lambda, and derives kappa <= beta otimes lambda = lambda, contradicting lambda < kappa. The equality beta otimes lambda = lambda follows from L5 (giving lambda otimes lambda = lambda) and L6 (monotonicity giving the upper bound, the trivial injection giving the lower bound) — terse but licensed by the cited facts. Step 3.1 correctly classifies infinite cardinals below aleph_omega as aleph_0 or aleph_{n+1}, all regular under AC. The title matches the statement, the remarks are accurate, and cross-references to sibling and companion items (cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power, fs-every-aleph-is-regular, fs-the-continuum-has-cardinality-aleph-omega, rem-cardinal-arithmetic-choice-ledger) are consistent.","at":"2026-07-28T19:13:20.300Z"}
