research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl:167:{"id":"ex-the-rationals-are-totally-disconnected-and-not-discrete","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified all four claims and their proof steps against the cited facts: step 1.1 correctly uses transitivity of subspace topology [A2] and order-convexity characterization [A1]; step 1.2 correctly produces a rational q'≠q in any open W containing q using [A2,A3,A4]; step 2.1 correctly derives at-most-one-point connected subsets from order-convexity plus irrational density [A3], then C(q)={q} from [A5]; step 2.2 correctly concludes non-discreteness from [A7] and non-openness of components; step 3.1 correctly shows local connectedness fails by taking U=Q and noting the only connected candidate {q} is not open. All [A1]–[A7] faithfully restate their cited items. Title matches what is proved. No contradictions with sibling items.","at":"2026-07-28T19:14:14.289Z"}
