research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-170-{"id":"fs-compact-implies-sequentially-compact","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"The refutation correctly constructs the witness Y = prod_{x in D} {0,1} with D = {0,1}^N, proves Y compact via Tychonoff [L1], assumes sequential compactness for contradiction, extracts a convergent subsequence F_{n_j} -> G, diagonalizes by defining x in D that alternates 0/1 on the subsequence indices, and derives a contradiction because the subbasic open set pi_x^{-1}[{G(x)}] must eventually contain F_{n_j} but F_{n_j}(x) is not eventually constant. All [L#] facts faithfully restate their cited sources, every step is licensed by its cited facts, and the diagonal construction is well-defined because the index map is injective.","at":"2026-07-28T19:15:05.914Z"}
