research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl:175:{"id":"cex-components-differ-from-quasicomponents","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the full proof: each S_n is connected (image of [0,1] under a continuous map), clopen in X (isolated by a strip), and no two-point subset of the projection P is order-convex (midpoints between consecutive reciprocals lie outside P). C(a)={a} follows because any connected E through a has order-convex projection in P, hence singleton {0}, forcing E into the discrete subspace {a,b}. Q(a)⊆{a,b} follows because each X∖S_n is clopen containing a. b∈Q(a) follows because any clopen K containing a catches S_m for all large m (by openness and Archimedean), swallows each whole segment (by [A4]), and being closed contains the limit of their top endpoints b. All [A1]–[A6] faithfully restate their cited items, and no contradictions with siblings or the companion page were found.","at":"2026-07-28T19:15:51.289Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-176-{"id":"fs-countably-compact-implies-compact","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"The refutation is logically valid: it assumes the false claim [A1], uses [L1] and [L2] (which faithfully restate claims 3 of thm-ordinal-spaces-and-compactness and claims 2,3,4 of thm-the-long-line-is-countably-compact-and-not-compact respectively) to establish that both omega_1 and the closed long ray are countably compact under countable choice, derives that both would be compact under [A1], then notes neither is compact, yielding a contradiction. All citations are faithful to the supplied source texts, the proof steps follow from the cited facts, and the remarks' cross-references to siblings (fs-sequentially-compact-implies-compact, thm-compactness-variants-hierarchy claim 1(b)) are accurate.","at":"2026-07-28T19:15:54.725Z"}
