research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-178-{"id":"fs-local-compactness-is-hereditary","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"The refutation is correct: it assumes the false claim, takes Q in the locally compact space R, derives that 0 has a compact neighbourhood K in Q containing (-eps,eps) cap Q, transfers K's compactness to R via [L4] (subspace topology transitivity), applies Heine-Borel via [L5] to get K closed in R, then uses density of Q and the irrationals via [L3] to find an irrational t in (0,eps) every neighbourhood of which meets K, forcing t in K subset Q by closedness — a contradiction. Every [L#] fact faithfully restates its cited source, every step is licensed by its tags, and the witness is the standard correct one.","at":"2026-07-28T19:16:34.170Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-179-{"id":"fs-local-compactness-is-hereditary","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the refutation step by step: R is locally compact by Heine-Borel (L2), assuming heredity makes Q locally compact (step 2.1), a compact neighbourhood K of 0 in Q contains (-ε,ε)∩Q, K is compact in R hence closed (steps 3.1, L4, L5), density of Q and irrationals (L3) forces an irrational t in (0,ε) whose every neighbourhood meets K, so t∈K⊆Q—contradiction. All [L#] facts faithfully restate their cited items, cross-references to thm-locally-compact-hausdorff-basics claim 2 and the companion page ex-sigma-compactness-and-lindelof-in-the-line-and-the-rationals are accurate, and the title matches what is proved.","at":"2026-07-28T19:16:34.967Z"}
